---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
---
<Shell title="Your private invitation">
<script is:inline slot="head">window.__inviteToken = new URLSearchParams(location.hash.slice(1)).get('token'); history.replaceState(null, '', location.pathname);</script>
<main id="main" class="invite-page"><a href="/" class="brand"><span class="brand-mark">c<span>h</span></span><span>content hub<span class="brand-sub">THE CLIENT SPACE</span></span></a><section class="invite-card panel"><span class="eyebrow">AN INVITATION TO YOUR WORKSPACE</span><h1>Let’s bring the<br/>picture into focus<span>.</span></h1><p>You’ve been invited to view results for the accounts or projects shared with your email address.</p><div class="scope-box"><strong>View. Understand. Stay in the loop.</strong><p>This is read-only access to your assigned targets. It does not allow editing metrics, publishing content, or viewing other clients’ work.</p></div><p id="invite-status" class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking your invitation…</p><button id="begin-invite" class="primary" hidden>Accept invitation & email a code <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><form id="code-form" hidden><label for="code">Verification code</label><p class="small">If the invitation is valid, a code was sent to its email address. Enter it below to finish accepting.</p><input id="code" name="code" type="text" inputmode="text" autocapitalize="none" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="one-time-code" pattern="[a-f0-9]{16}" maxlength="16" required placeholder="16-character code"/><button class="primary" type="submit">Verify & open workspace <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></form><p class="small">If your link has expired, been revoked, or this step was interrupted, ask your workspace administrator for a fresh invitation. Never forward your invitation or verification code.</p><a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Content Hub</a></section><p class="invite-footnote">A private space for the work you’re building.</p></main>
<script>import '../scripts/invite';</script>
</Shell>
